title: '[pallet-revive] Add unstable runtime precompile (call dispatch + raw storage reads)'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Adds the opt-in, feature-gated `UnstableRuntime` precompile to `pallet-revive`,
      exposing two low-level primitives to contracts:

      - `dispatch(bytes)` — dispatch an arbitrary SCALE-encoded `RuntimeCall` as the
        calling contract's account (a `Signed` origin).
      - `getStorage(bytes, uint32)` — read the raw bytes of any runtime storage item
        by its full key.

      The precompile is gated behind the new, default-off `unstable-precompiles`
      cargo feature and must be explicitly added to a runtime's `Config::Precompiles`
      to become active. Its interface is unstable — pallet indices, call encodings
      and storage keys may change across runtime upgrades — and must not be enabled
      on production runtimes. A configurable `Filter: Contains<RuntimeCall>` type
      parameter (default `Everything`) lets a runtime restrict which calls may be
      dispatched. Both primitives are weight-metered with dedicated benchmarks.

crates:
  # `validate: false`: the SemVer check cannot build rustdoc JSON for these crates
  # because the `pallet-revive-fixtures` build script compiles contracts with
  # `-Z json-target-spec` (rustc 1.95+), which the SemVer toolchain rejects. The
  # declared bumps are intentionally conservative (`major`).
  - name: pallet-revive
    bump: major
    validate: false
  - name: pallet-revive-fixtures
    bump: major
    validate: false
